# check_deno_types.allowlist — pre-existing TypeScript errors as of 2026-05-06
# class-kill A ship.
#
# Format: <relative_path> <error_count_baseline>
# One file per line. Comments start with #.
#
# COMMENT POLICY (mirrors B4 grep allowlist):
#   - Adding new entries requires James approval.
#   - Removing entries: verify the underlying error is fixed (count → 0)
#     before removing the entry.
#   - Reducing baseline: when partial fix lowers count, update baseline
#     to reflect new floor.
#
# Why these are allowlisted (not fixed):
#   170 pre-existing TS errors across 43 files when class kill A shipped.
#   Mostly inherited from 7 root-cause errors in _shared/* (each consumer
#   that imports a broken shared module sees the propagated error). Fixing
#   the 170 errors is a separate cleanup project, not the discipline-shipping
#   work. Allowlist baselines lock today's count; future PRs can't regress
#   any file's count without explicit allowlist amendment.
#
# Per-file baseline counts captured 2026-05-06 17:54Z, deno 2.7.14.

